From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:46:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] HID: dockchannel: let keyboard input and trackpad
 clicks wake the system

The suspend-to-idle filter wakes the system with pm_wakeup_hard_event()
on a keyboard report or a trackpad click, but nothing enables wakeup
for the device, and that call does nothing while wakeup is disabled, as
it is by default for a platform device. A keypress or a click does not
end suspend-to-idle until something in user space enables wakeup in
sysfs, while the SMC's lid and power button input enables its own at
probe.

Enable wakeup at probe. The receive interrupt already runs through the
sleep (IRQF_NO_SUSPEND) and the filter is unchanged, so only a key or a
click ends it. Wakeup can still be turned off in sysfs.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/hid/dockchannel-hid/dockchannel-hid.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/hid/dockchannel-hid/dockchannel-hid.c b/drivers/hid/dockchannel-hid/dockchannel-hid.c
index 2688654551..ea7457486d 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/dockchannel-hid/dockchannel-hid.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/dockchannel-hid/dockchannel-hid.c
@@ -1765,6 +1765,16 @@ static int dockchannel_hid_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return -EIO;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * A keypress or a trackpad click ends suspend-to-idle through
+	 * pm_wakeup_hard_event(), which does nothing while wakeup is disabled,
+	 * as it is by default for a platform device. Enable it, as the SMC's
+	 * lid and power button input does; sysfs can still turn it off.
+	 */
+	ret = devm_device_init_wakeup(dev);
+	if (ret)
+		dev_warn(dev, "keyboard and trackpad cannot wake the system: %d\n", ret);
+
 	dev_dbg(dchid->dev, "Initialized, awaiting packets\n");
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, dchid);
 	dockchannel_await(dchid->dc, dchid_handle_packet, dchid, sizeof(struct dchid_hdr));
-- 
